// ★★ THE DESK — four classic λ programs, computed by the machine, then separated by SHAPE
//    and selected by a PREDICATE.
//
//   plus 2 3      ⟶β  λf.λx. f(f(f(f(f x))))   Church 5   — body is an APPLICATION
//   mult 2 3      ⟶β  λf.λx. f(f(f(f(f(f x)))))Church 6   — body is an APPLICATION
//   not true      ⟶β  λt.λf. f                 FALSE      — body is a VARIABLE
//   and true true ⟶β  λt.λf. t                 TRUE       — body is a VARIABLE
//
// Church numerals and Church booleans are BOTH two-binder terms, so a pattern that only
// counted binders could not tell them apart. `lam f. lam x. (f, ${rest})` can: it requires
// the body to be an application of the OUTER binder, which every numeral ≥ 1 is and no
// boolean is. The booleans are refused structurally and left resting.
//
// Nothing below spells an answer. Every payload arrives because `[*]` explored the program.

@"results"!(lambda:Term`((lam m. lam n. lam f. lam x. ((m, f), ((n, f), x)), lam f. lam x. (f, (f, x))), lam f. lam x. (f, (f, (f, x))))`)[*] |
@"results"!(lambda:Term`((lam m. lam n. lam f. (m, (n, f)), lam f. lam x. (f, (f, x))), lam f. lam x. (f, (f, (f, x))))`)[*] |
@"results"!(lambda:Term`(lam b. ((b, lam t. lam f. f), lam t. lam f. t), lam t. lam f. t)`)[*] |
@"results"!(lambda:Term`((lam p. lam q. ((p, q), p), lam t. lam f. t), lam t. lam f. t)`)[*] |

for(@lambda:Term`lam f. lam x. (f, ${rest})` <- @"results") {
  @"OUT"!(lambda:Term`${rest}`)
}
